@page "/kanban/default-functionalities"

@using Syncfusion.Blazor.KanbanDemo
@using Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban
@*Hidden:Lines*@
@inherits SampleBaseComponent;
@*End:Hidden*@

<ActionDescription>
<p>
    This sample demonstrates the default functionalities of the <a class="e-kanban-default-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the explore Syncfusion Blazor Kanban component"
                                                                                                     href="https://www.syncfusion.com/gantt-sdk/blazor-kanban-board"
                                                                                                     target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blazor Kanban</a> component by visualizing a Coffee Roastery Batches. By default, cards can be dragged and dropped across all columns, and the board renders with the minimal configuration required for the component.
</p>
<p>
    The sample uses the minimal configuration required to render the Kanban board and cards. Essential settings include <a class="e-kanban-default-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of DataSource property in Kanban"
                                                                                                     href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.SfKanban-1.html#Syncfusion_Blazor_Kanban_SfKanban_1_DataSource"
                                                                                                     target="_blank" rel="noopener">DataSource</a>, <a class="e-kanban-default-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of KanbanColumns"
                                                                                                     href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.KanbanColumns.html"
                                                                                                     target="_blank" rel="noopener">KanbanColumns</a>, and <a class="e-kanban-default-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the API reference of KanbanCardSettings"
                                                                                                     href="https://help.syncfusion.com/cr/blazor/Syncfusion.Blazor.Kanban.KanbanCardSettings.html"
                                                                                                     target="_blank" rel="noopener">KanbanCardSettings</a>.
</p>
<p>
    Additional essential interactions that enhance analysis and control are also featured:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the drag and drop in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/drag-and-drop"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Drag and Drop</a>: Move cards between columns to update their workflow status with a single action.
    </li>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the columns in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/columns"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Columns</a>: Group cards by workflow stage such as Open, In Progress, Testing, and Close.
    </li>
    <li>
        <a aria-label="Navigate to the documentation for the card settings in the kanban component"
           href="https://blazor.syncfusion.com/documentation/kanban/cards"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Card Settings</a>: Map the title, summary, tags, and footer image to display rich card content.
    </li>
</ul>
<p>
    Key interactive features demonstrated in this sample include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Drag and Drop</b>: Click and hold any card to drag it across columns. The board updates status as soon as the card is dropped.</li>
    <li><b>Card Footer</b>: Each card displays type, priority, and assignee avatars using built-in CSS field mappings.</li>
    <li><b>Tag Visualization</b>: Tags appear as colored chips on each card for quick scanning of categories.</li>
    <li><b>Auto Layout</b>: Columns are automatically sized to fit the available board width without any manual configuration.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    The <b>Board Configuration</b> highlights the minimum property surface needed to render a fully functional Kanban:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>DataSource</b>: Binds the task collection that supplies the cards rendered on the board.</li>
    <li><b>KeyField</b>: Maps the data field that determines which column a card belongs to.</li>
    <li><b>KanbanColumns</b>: Declares the column collection using header text and a matching key field.</li>
    <li><b>KanbanCardSettings</b>: Configures the header, content, footer image, and tag fields on each card.</li>
</ul>
<p>
Looking for the full Blazor Kanban component overview, features, pricing, and documentation? Visit the <a class="e-kanban-default-reference-link" aria-label="Navigate to the explore Syncfusion Blazor Kanban component" href="https://www.syncfusion.com/gantt-sdk/blazor-kanban-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blazor Kanban</a> page.</p>
</ActionDescription>


<div class="col-lg-12 control-section">
    <SfKanban KeyField="Status" DataSource="@CardData" Height="500px">
        <KanbanColumns>
            @foreach (ColumnModel item in ColumnData)
            {
                <KanbanColumn HeaderText="@item.HeaderText" KeyField="@item.KeyField"/>
            }
        </KanbanColumns>
        <KanbanCardSettings HeaderField="Title" ContentField="Summary" TagsField="CardTags">
            <Template>
                @{
                    KanbanDataModel card = (KanbanDataModel)context;
                    <div class="default-kanban-card" style="border-left-color: @card.Color;">
                        <div class="dkc-header">
                            <div class="dkc-id">@card.Id</div>
                            <div class="dkc-priority" data-priority="@card.Priority">
                                <span class="dkc-priority-dot"></span>
                                @card.Priority
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="dkc-title">@card.Title</div>
                        <div class="dkc-content">@card.Summary</div>
                        <div class="dkc-tags">
                            @if (card.CardTags != null)
                            {
                                @foreach (string tag in card.CardTags)
                                {
                                    <span class="dkc-tag">@tag</span>
                                }
                            }
                        </div>
                        <div class="dkc-footer">
                            <div class="dkc-type">
                                <span class="dkc-icon dkc-icon-type"></span>
                                <span>@card.Type</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
            </Template>
        </KanbanCardSettings>
    </SfKanban>
</div>

